{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WFcuafoCYq1GYbWvntpbky","type":"tool_result","content":"CHANGELOG.md:5:`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\nCHANGELOG.md:7:When a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\nCHANGELOG.md:20:  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader\nCHANGELOG.md:21:  (`assets`, `setAssetReader`) no longer sees the files the kit embeds (`__PIXEL_ASSETS__`: the\nCHANGELOG.md:408:  bundled; it resolves to a `ModelCatalog` (`into` also adds the defs to one of yours).\nCHANGELOG.md:412:  Anyone else's work, CC0 included and a single file too, only from a pack (`source.pack`) whose\nCHANGELOG.md:821:- **The engine kit**: `npm run bundle` builds `pixel-engine.js`, one self-contained ES module\nGUIDE.md:28:- **Serve it over HTTP.** ES modules don't load from `file://`. Any static server works:\nGUIDE.md:41:  (paths are relative to the page). To ship one file with no `assets/` folder, set\nGUIDE.md:42:  `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__ = { 'assets/ship.glb': 'data:model/gltf-binary;base64,...' }`\nGUIDE.md:135:    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\nGUIDE.md:1005:| Blank page, console: CORS / \"Failed to load module script\" | opened with `file://` | serve the folder over HTTP |\nGUIDE.md:1006:| Console: \"Multiple instances of Three.js being imported\" | three.js loaded twice | use `THREE` from the bundle, nothing else |\nAPI.md:45:Models every bundle carries: `ctx.loadModel('assets/hero.glb')` works with no files next to it.\nAPI.md:2743:- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is full, 0 for an unknown preset). Inline preset objects share one emitter per distinct content, so `burst({ ...literal }, at)` every…\nAPI.md:2857:(`__PIXEL_ASSETS__`: the kit's built-in models) never reach it, as they never reach a page's fetch.\nAPI.md:3030:base URL; a page may put a data URL for it in `__PIXEL_ASSETS__`, as single-file builds do for\nAPI.md:3074:The library's families (one file each, src/engine/model/library/<family>.ts) in order: each\n----\n5:  {\"id\":\"kenney-castle\",\"title\":\"Kenney Castle Kit 2.0\",\"about\":\"Kenney Castle Kit 2.0 by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/castle-kit)\",\"file\":\"packs/kenney-castle.json\",\"models\":76,\"textures\":0,\"licence\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"author\":\"Kenney\",\"homepage\":\"https://kenney.nl/assets/castle-kit\",\"url\":\"https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/castle-kit/a395102d20-1711543616/kenney_castle-kit.zip\"},\n6:  {\"id\":\"kenney-furniture\",\"title\":\"Kenney Furniture Kit 2.0\",\"about\":\"Kenney Furniture Kit 2.0 by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/furniture-kit)\",\"file\":\"packs/kenney-furniture.json\",\"models\":140,\"textures\":0,\"licence\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"author\":\"Kenney\",\"homepage\":\"https://kenney.nl/assets/furniture-kit\",\"url\":\"https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/furniture-kit/440e0608a4-1677580847/kenney_furniture-kit.zip\"},\n7:  {\"id\":\"kenney-mini-dungeon\",\"title\":\"Kenney Mini Dungeon 2.0\",\"about\":\"Kenney Mini Dungeon 2.0 by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/mini-dungeon)\",\"file\":\"packs/kenney-mini-dungeon.json\",\"models\":30,\"textures\":0,\"licence\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"author\":\"Kenney\",\"homepage\":\"https://kenney.nl/assets/mini-dungeon\",\"url\":\"https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/mini-dungeon/6cd72dc849-1785314274/kenney_mini-dungeon.zip\"},\n8:  {\"id\":\"kenney-nature\",\"title\":\"Kenney Nature Kit 2.1\",\"about\":\"Kenney Nature Kit 2.1 by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/nature-kit)\",\"file\":\"packs/kenney-nature.json\",\"models\":329,\"textures\":0,\"licence\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"author\":\"Kenney\",