ossing: Let’s Go to the City\",\"url\":\"https://nintendo.com/en-gb/Games/Wii/Animal-Crossing-Let-s-Go-to-the-City-280484.html\"},{\"title\":\"Animal Crossing: City Folk\",\"url\":\"https://wiki.kidzsearch.com/wiki/Animal_Crossing_City_Folk\"},{\"title\":\"Animal Crossing: City Folk\",\"url\":\"https://retro-replay.com/db/wii/animal-crossing-city-folk\"},{\"title\":\"Animal Crossing: City Folk\",\"url\":\"https://gamingfurever.com/games/genre/rpg/animal-crossing-city-folk\"},{\"title\":\"top of page\",\"url\":\"https://www.extralifegaming.net/product-page/animal-crossing-city-folk\"}]\n\nCity Folk is the Wii entry in the series, and its main additions are the city and Wii Speak. Here's an overview from the search results:\n\n- **Wii Speak:** The game was the first Wii title to support the Wii Speak microphone accessory, which enables voice chat over Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection (6-3, 6-9). Players can chat with friends while visiting each other's towns (10-10).\n- **The city:** This is the new shopping hub, reached from your town by bus (8-3, 10-6). Shops there include GracieGrace for limited-edition clothing and furniture (16-8), and the city also has an auction house (15-2).\n- **Tom Nook and the home loan:** Nook provides and finances your house, and you can pay it off over time (6-7, 6-8). Early on, Nook gives you part-time chores that pay down the initial loan (10-8).\n- **Shopping and selling:** Furniture comes from Tom Nook's shop, Redd's in the city, or other villagers (7-7). Nook also buys items you no longer want (16-6).\n- **Carry-over:** The DS Suitcase feature lets you bring your character and furniture catalog over from Wild World (2-3).\n- **Reception:** Reviews were mixed, and the game has sold 3.38 million copies worldwide (6-4, 6-12).\n\nThe sources are mostly wiki and fan-run sites, so specific details like shop names and prices may vary by version. I couldn't confirm everything from the official Nintendo page, which covers only the main features.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b81aee7-e493-4131-b722-c7c742e27493","uuid":"af264ec6-ce71-4b9e-8840-390dce20416b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:48:09.602Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Animal Crossing: City Folk features the City bus shops Wii Speak Tom Nook gameplay overview","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PjXiWbKWDtGF9wzKCox65T","content":[{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_Crossing:_City_Folk"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Animal_Crossing_City_Folk"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-21096/"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Animal_Crossing_City_Folk/Releases"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-21096"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_Crossing_(Wii)"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://ipfs.aleph.im/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Animal_Crossing_(Wii).html"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://nookipedia.com/wiki/City_Folk"},{"title":"animal crossing city folk","url":"https://www.timeextension.com/games/wii/animal_crossing_city_folk"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk | ||","url":"https://animalcrossing.fandom.com/wiki/Animal_crossing:_City_Folk"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk","url":"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Animal_Crossing%3A_City_Folk"},{"title":"GamesRadar+ Verdict","url":"https://gamesradar.com/animal-crossing-city-folk-review"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk Updated Hands-On","url":"https://www.gamespot.com/articles/animal-crossing-city-folk-updated-hands-on/1100-6198525/"},{"title":"Animal Crossing: City Folk - Nintendo Wii","url":"https://shop.drea