{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkiFdrxaqB1PD1VMh6bx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WYVMGz7tuf5HQi8KvTgoKA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162054__x00d3db/work && python3 - <<'PY'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# --- verified table: browser flags\nrep(\"| One HTML on `file://`, WebGPU on | Works. Boots in 1–2 s on the software GPU. Inline modules avoid the `file://` module ban the guide warns about. |\",\n\"| **Browser flags for WebGPU here** | **The engine needs `--use-angle=swiftshader`.** With only `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, as TASK.md lists them, it never renders: the device is lost (`Instance dropped in popErrorScope`), `gpuRecoveries` climbs, the frame count sticks, the picture stays blank. Use the kit's own `check.mjs` set: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. |\\n| One HTML on `file://`, WebGPU on | Works. Boots in 1–2 s on the software GPU. Inline modules avoid the `file://` module ban the guide warns about. |\")\n\n# --- packaging size note\nrep(\"This keeps the engine exactly as it ships, as TASK.md and the guide require: a test asserts its text appears unchanged in the page. Everything is inline, with no network at runtime.\",\n\"This keeps the engine exactly as it ships, as TASK.md and the guide require: a test asserts its text appears unchanged in the page. Everything is inline, with no network at runtime. With both packs the page is about 8 MB before your game's code; trimming packs to the models you name is optional.\")\n\n# --- camera tween + movement basis\nrep(\"Zoom 1.6 gives 32 art pixels a metre, about 15 m across and 15 m of ground depth. Catch a failed start\",\n\"Zoom 1.6 gives 32 art pixels a metre, about 15 m across and 15 m of ground depth. To turn or zoom, tween with `engine.setCamera({ preset:'iso', yaw, pitch:35, zoom:z, minZoom:z, maxZoom:z }, { syncUrl:false })`. Keep movement camera-relative with `ctx.camera.groundBasis()`, so all four turns play the same. Catch a failed start\")\n\n# --- jump gag: there is no jump button\nrep(\"A jump press gets a once-per-session gag: *\\\"You can't jump. You're in escrow.\\\"*\",\n\"Pressing the tool button with empty hands gets a once-per-session gag: *\\\"You can't jump. You're in escrow.\\\"*\")\n\n# --- real clock completeness\nrep(\"Sunday is Market Day; Saturday is Show Day; the contest falls on the second Wednesday of the season's middle month, the festival on its last Saturday.\",\n\"Sunday is Market Day, Saturday is Show Day, other days are Errand Days; the contest falls on the second Wednesday of the season's middle month, the festival on its last Saturday.\")\n\n# --- cheese: seasons, not weeks\nrep(\"pattern per week: Rising, Falling, Wobble or Spike (peak 3–6×)\",\"pattern per season: Rising, Falling, Wobble or Spike (peak 3–6×)\")\n\n# --- letters wording\nrep(\"Mail arrives at 09:00: neighbour letters (with presents, per friendship), Gran's weekly passive-aggressive note with a foreign fruit or something inexplicable, museum thanks, Bureau results, catalogue orders, Hub of gossip.\",\n\"Mail arrives at 09:00: neighbour letters (with presents, per friendship), Gran's passive-aggressive note each season with a foreign fruit or something inexplicable, museum thanks, Bureau results, catalogue orders, the occasional anonymous tip from Ozzie.\")\n\n# --- day 2 tools\nrep(\"| 2 | Spring, Errand | Museum opens with your fossil; Axe and Slingshot; first City trip |\",\n\"| 2 | Spring, Errand | Museum opens with your fossil; Axe and Slingshot go on sale at the store; first City trip |\")\n\n# --- bloom verified\nrep(\"**Bloom's default strength blows out characters and glass** [verified]: start at `{ id: 'bloom', params: { amount: 0.3 } }` and tune by eye, City nights only, swapped under a transition.\",\n\"**Bloom's default strength blows out characters and glass; `{ id: 'bloom', params: { amount: 0.3 } }` in the look's `scene` stack keeps them readable** [verified by render]. City nights only, swapped under a transition.\")\n\n# --- day one closing line\nrep(\"Every errand is a demonstration of a verb. Skipping none is fine, wandering off is fine: the list waits.\",\n\"Every errand demonstrates a verb. Wandering off is fine: the list waits.\")\n\n# --- hourly tunes row\nrep(\"| **Hourly tunes:** a different one for every hour, each with rain and snow variants, built by `composer.js` from hand-written motifs (transposition, tempo, re-voicing) | 24 hours from 8 motifs → 12 |\",\n\"| **Hourly tunes:** every one of the 24 hours has its own arrangement, each with rain and snow variants, built by `composer.js` from hand-written motifs (transposition, tempo, re-voicing) | 8 → 12 motifs |\")\n\n# --- hub sources + null connect + robust card key\nrep(\"Follow `lib/hub/README.md` (AI Hub Session Protocol v1). Two modes share one host/guest code path\",\n\"Follow `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md` (AI Hub Session Protocol v1); `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` sit beside it. Two modes share one host/guest code path\")\nrep(\"with no key press.\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\"\",\n\"with no key press. If `connect()` answers `null`, there's no hub after all: carry on with the normal start.\\n\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\"\")\nrep(\"Nothing else on the card; it changes nothing.\",\n\"Nothing else on the card; it changes nothing. Read Enter with a plain `keydown` listener on `window`: the harness pokes a synthetic key and allows 3 s, and software-rendered frames can be slow.\")\n\n# --- Visit wording\nrep(\"A guest arrives by bus in the host's town. Same avatars, tools and neighbours; Host's world is authoritative.\",\n\"A guest arrives by bus in the host's town. Same avatars, tools and neighbours; the host's world is authoritative.\")\n\n# --- browser suite flags + visit suite wording\nrep(\"| **browser** | Chromium on `file://` the built HTML, with the flags in TASK.md |\",\n\"| **browser** | Chromium on `file://` the built HTML, with the flags from section 2 (not TASK.md's shorter list) |\")\nrep(\"BroadcastChannel join and movement seen on both; WebRTC with `iceServers: []` join, invite codes round trip; a game saved, reloaded on both |\",\n\"BroadcastChannel join and movement seen on both; WebRTC with `iceServers: []` join, invite codes round trip; after leaving, the guest keeps pockets and beans and the host's save is unchanged |\")\n\n# --- coverage table: this computer\nrep(\"| Performance out of scope, unlimited budget | Sections 16, 22 |\",\n\"| This computer, its stand-ins, sharing it | Sections 2, 22 (and one correction: browser flags, section 2) |\\n| Performance out of scope, unlimited budget | Sections 16, 22 |\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\nPY\ngrep -n -i -E \"gametitle|exit-interview|claude-opus|\\.html\\b|mabel|tom nook\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-140; echo \"--- words:\"; wc -w PLAN.md; wc -c PLAN.md; grep -n \"^## \" PLAN.md","description":"Apply review fixes to the plan and check it for forbidden names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4374,"cache_read_input_tokens":444550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4374},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b81aee7-e493-4131-b722-c7c742e27493","uuid":"73fad4a7-b500-407d-a105-8f