 the source distinctive without recreating it: the mechanics stay, but every name, character, species-for-role pairing, melody and layout had to be new, and the replacements still had to be funny.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Correct the WebGPU flags in 'This computer', or point to the set in the kit's check.mjs; as written, a builder's first browser run shows a blank screen. Note that python3 -m http.server prints its port only when unbuffered, so a script reading it through a pipe needs -u. State plainly whether multiplayer outside the Hub is required, and the minimum if so. Tell the planner the builders' model, effort and rough time budget, and how many hours 'long enough to show ALL features' should mean, since scope depends on all of these. Say outright that a planner may prototype in a scratch folder, because that is where the most useful findings came from. Finally, mark which TASK.md sections are for the builder only, so the planner knows what the plan must carry and what it can leave to them.\"\n  }\n]\nJSON\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json'));print('interview ok',len(d),[q['question'] for q in d])\"; T=\"$PWD/_scratch\"; case \"$T\" in */x00d3db/work/_scratch) ps -eo pid,comm --no-headers | awk '$2 ~ /^(python3|chrome|headless_shell|node)$/ {print $1}' | while read pid; do c=$(readlink /proc/$pid/cwd 2>/dev/null); case \"$c\" in \"$T\"*) echo \"still running in scratch: $pid $(ps -o comm= -p $pid)\";; esac; done; du -sh \"$T\" | cut -f1; rm -rf -- \"$T\" && echo \"scratch removed\";; esac; ls -la; git status --short . | head","description":"Validate plan tables, save the exit interview, and remove my scratch folder"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01LhrNbC2gfzNjSWrzGGHuSP":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162054__x00d3db/work"}}}
